  "question": {
    "text": "Ice starts forming in a lake where the water is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and the ambient temperature is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. If the time taken for <math><mn>1</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>c</mn><mn>m</mn></math> of ice to be formed is&nbsp;<math><mi>7 hours</mi></math>, then the time taken for the thickness of ice to change from <math><mn>1</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>c</mn><mn>m</mn></math> to <math><mn>2</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>c</mn><mn>m</mn></math> is",
